Z||000000||pontiacs4me||03-06-2001||02:12 AM||||My 2.8 liter is driving me crazy.  When I start up the car the belt squalls for about 5 seconds or until I rev it up a little and let it idle back down it stops.  It did this last week all the time.  Everywhere I drove it squalled so I put a new alternator and alt bracket on it.  (I broke the big alt. bolt a few weeks back and only the stud and the tensioner adjust bolt was holding it in there.  But is sat a bit crooked.  So I put a new bracket on there and no noise, for about 2 days, then today it started squalling again. Could I of ruined this belt from it squalling all the time, last week?  Is there any thing Im overlooking?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||03-06-2001||02:19 AM||||Some big auto chains supply the wrong sized belt.  Believe me, its happened to me twice at 2 different ones.  I finally ordered one from the Fiero Store and it was the right size.||||reg||14
Z||000002||Bugsy||03-06-2001||10:27 AM||||watch your amp guage when you start it up, my 2.8 had the same symptom...on initial startup the alt wasn't charging.  when the alt kicked in, the squeal stopped<P>------------------<BR>86 SE I'm addicted and proud of it<BR>Kevin||||reg||6
Z||000003||My7Fieros||03-06-2001||02:02 PM||||Ahh yes, very common Fiero problem. One answer, <B>DAYCO</B> brand alt belt...it works, believe me!!!!!!!!!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||2birds||03-06-2001||09:37 PM||||I run Goodyear Gatorback belts, about $15 from Summitt Racing.  Make sure you don't have any oil or anti-freeze (water pump seal) leaks.  The balancer/front cover seal was my source of squeal.  See my info in the timing chain replacement thread.||||reg||1
Z||000005||pontiacs4me||03-07-2001||04:10 PM||||I fixed it,  I bought a new belt and tightened it with the lug wrench, between the slide on the alt bracket and the rear shock mount.  I gave it all I had to get it tight.  It doesnt make a peep now, and I found the bonging device under the dash, its history now.  thanks.||||reg||1
